Subject: [PATCH 07208/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-26/27: fix
 refactor_prompt's invalid-JSON bug (doesn't fully resolve round 2) + ship
 mandatory truncation detection

REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-26: before applying the operator's suggested codeonly-
directive fix to refactor_prompt(), checked _gen_to_file's own comments
first and found that exclusion is DELIBERATE (refactor is a documented
reasoning task, must not be told to skip all reasoning, 2026-06-25) --
applying the suggested fix would have silently reverted a considered
design choice. Investigated further and found the real bug instead:
refactor_prompt's mismatch encoding sliced json.dumps(...) by raw
character count AFTER encoding -- verified 5 real g50t mismatches
serialize to 12,212 chars, and [:4000] cuts mid-field-name, producing
genuinely invalid JSON shown to the LLM. Fixed via _bounded_mismatches()
(caps cell-diff lists before encoding, with an honest omitted-count
field) -- an unconditional bug fix that also improves the already-
shipped level_up_reinduction path, since refactor_prompt is shared.

Live re-run WITH the fix: round 2 still fails. Baseline gets the
identical failure message as before the fix (refuting invalid JSON as
the sole cause); sge gets a NEW failure, a direct 300s TimeoutError.
Both data points point toward generation time/length as the real
bottleneck, not input validity.

REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-27 (operator directive: "should we increase max
context? we must always detect reaching max context truncation"):
generate()/complete_text() previously read only response.get("content")
from llama.cpp's completion response, silently discarding stop_type
("limit" = cut off by n_predict before finishing, confirmed live via a
direct probe) and truncated (prompt itself overflowed n_ctx). Added
last_stop_type/last_prompt_truncated instance attributes + a
_record_completion_diagnostics() helper wired into both completion
paths (return contracts unchanged); generate()'s failure message now
names the specific cause when detected. This ships the instrumentation;
the next live run will confirm whether stop_type=="limit" is actually
occurring before deciding whether to raise max_tokens.

8 new tests total across both REQs.

